From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: ntdll, kernelbase: RegRestoreKey restores a hive over a key

NtRestoreKey and RegRestoreKeyW were stubs reporting success. Windows
replaces the key's values and subkeys with those of the hive's root key.
Click-to-Run publishes Office's virtual registry with it (its MSI component
paths, COM classes and file associations); with the stub the virtual
registry stayed empty, Office could not find its own components ("this
feature appears to be broken"), and its Windows App SDK sign-in page never
loaded.

A hive is a Windows binary hive ("regf": base block, hbins, nk/vk records,
lf/lh/li/ri subkey lists, big data in db segments; compressed and UTF-16
names) or a file in Wine's own text format, which NtSaveKey writes -- that
one is loaded under a scratch key, copied, and the scratch key removed.
REG_WHOLE_HIVE_VOLATILE makes the restored keys volatile. The file is
untrusted: every offset, length and nesting depth is checked, and a file
that is not a hive is refused (STATUS_REGISTRY_CORRUPT).

Gate: test/regrestore-gate.sh (make test-regrestore), with test/regf-write.py.

